# Coin Security ControlRoom Code Style Rules

## Backend (Laravel 12)
- Always use Laravel 12 conventions and patterns
- Follow PSR-12 coding standards
- Use type hints and return types on all methods
- Prefer dependency injection over facades where possible
- Use Eloquent relationships properly with eager loading to avoid N+1 issues

## Frontend (React + TypeScript)
- All frontend components must use React with TypeScript (.tsx format)
- Use functional components with hooks (no class components)
- Use Tailwind CSS for styling with the coin theme color palette
- Maintain dark mode consistency - never use light colors in dark mode
- Use mobile-first responsive design approach

## UI/UX Guidelines
- Use modals instead of create/show/edit pages for faster navigation
- All pages and modals must be mobile-first designed
- Maintain consistent dark mode theming throughout the application
- Use the coin color theme (coin-600, coin-700, coin-800, coin-900)
- Use shadcn/ui components where available

## Code Quality
- Delete all obsolete code and files whenever making changes
- Avoid reverting to previously changed code unless explicitly instructed
- Keep components small and focused (single responsibility)
- Add proper TypeScript types for all props and state
- Use proper error handling and loading states

## Project Structure
- Keep Laravel backend code in `app/` directory
- Keep React components in `resources/js/` directory
- Use Inertia.js for page routing
- Follow existing project conventions
